# Line endings, enforced by Git rather than by each editor.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is false in this checkout, so nothing used to convert anything
# and the tree accumulated two conventions (475 files with CRLF, 654 with LF).
# Editors that honour .editorconfig then rewrote a whole file on the first save,
# which is what "I saved and the formatting exploded" looked like.
#
# After this file lands, normalise the working tree once:
#
#     git add --renormalize .
#     git status            # review; expect whole-file diffs only on CRLF files
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows scripts: PowerShell and cmd.exe want CRLF, and a lone LF changes how
# some of them parse.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never let Git's "text=auto" guess on these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.a binary
*.lib binary
*.exe binary
